  "question": {
    "text": "In a Frank - Hertz experiment, an electron of energy <math><mn>5.6</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi></math>&nbsp;passes through mercury vapour and emerges with an energy <math><mn>0.7</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The minimum wavelength of photons emitted by mercury atoms is close to:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>250</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>m</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>1700</mn><mi> </mi><mi>n</mi><mi>m</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>220</mn><mi> </mi><mi>n</mi><mi>m</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>2020</mn><mi> </mi><mi>n</mi><mi>m</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "When electron pass through the mercury vapor, it losses some of its energy. The loss in <math><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi></math> of electron <math><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#8901;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4.9</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> energy of radiation emitted <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>4.9</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> wavelength of radiation, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.24</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mo>&#215;</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4.9</mn></mfrac><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8776;</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mn>250</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>n</mi><mi>m</mi></math>"
  }
}